WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience applauds)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.770
- All right, let's close out the hour

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.330
with one last uplifting story.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.237
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.480
(exciting music)

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.170
(audience applauds)

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:08.003
As a mama.

00:00:08.003 --> 00:00:09.960
I would do anything to keep my kiddo safe.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.700
I'm hardly the only one.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.620
When one mom in Canada realized

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.120
there were no bicycle helmets

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:15.953
that properly fit

00:00:15.953 --> 00:00:17.430
over her son's top knots,

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:18.930
she did something about it.

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.510
She designed helmets that
would fit them just right

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.340
and she's a actually also selling them

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.500
to others in her situation as well.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.760
We have her on the line right now

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.530
watching on City TV, Toronto,

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:29.550
let's say "hi" to Tina.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:30.383
What's up, Tina?

00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:31.320
(audience applauds)

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.877
- Hi Kelly, I'm so excited to be here.

00:00:32.877 --> 00:00:34.740
- I'm so excited to have you.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.855
So this has been five
years in the making, right?

00:00:36.855 --> 00:00:39.570
- Yeah, so about five years ago

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.070
my oldest son was five years old

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.710
and we couldn't find any
bike helmets to fit him.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.990
We are a Sikh family,
and so my kids have long

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:48.000
uncut hair they wear in a top knot.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.020
And so for that reason,

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:50.580
a lot of traditional bike helmets

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.560
don't fit them in the
way that they need to.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.300
I'm an occupational therapist who worked

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.290
in the area of head injury

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:58.440
so I know how important bike helmets are

00:00:58.440 --> 00:00:59.910
and you know we've tried a lot

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:02.640
of creative solutions to get
something to work for our kids.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.710
We would hollow out the internal foam.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.950
Some people go as far as
cutting holes in their helmet.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.510
It was never quite the right solution

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:10.920
and I just wanted to make an option

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.810
for my kids where they never had to choose

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:16.140
between their identity
and sport participation.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.330
- Absolutely. So I love
that you took action.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:19.830
So how did you do it?

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:20.790
- Well, my husband and I

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:22.080
did a lot of research

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.700
and then we worked with an engineer.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.710
Once we had our design finalized,

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.180
we got a prototype.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:28.013
That prototype,

00:01:28.013 --> 00:01:29.460
we then tried on our kids,

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:30.660
all the neighborhood kids,

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:33.600
anyone we could find who
fell in that age bracket.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:35.220
And then we did more development,

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.053
more testing,

00:01:36.053 --> 00:01:36.930
and I'm happy to share

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.370
that we just wrapped up pre-sales.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:39.203
And so,

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:40.913
you know

00:01:40.913 --> 00:01:41.760
my kids are excited

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.590
to have a helmet that works for them

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:47.190
and I'm excited that, you know
I no longer have to nag them

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:48.180
about bike helmets.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:50.010
And it's been a real learning curve

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.680
and blessing to be able to
share with them from beginning

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.170
to end that you can take
an idea that you have

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.880
and follow through with the right support.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.740
- Absolutely.
(audience applauds)

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.420
What a great example you are.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.500
Thank you so much, Tina.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.229
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:03.229 --> 00:02:04.800
(bell dings)

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:05.943
- Oh, thank you.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.400
- That's a rad looking helmet.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.233
That's not all,

00:02:09.233 --> 00:02:10.066
our season long partner,

00:02:10.066 --> 00:02:11.280
Pilot pen makers of G2,

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.110
the go-to pin of the Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.750
Want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like you, ma'am.

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.340
So, they're gonna be writing you a check

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:18.240
for a thousand dollars.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.073
How's that sound?

00:02:19.073 --> 00:02:19.906
(audience applauds)

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.427
- Oh my gawd.

00:02:21.427 --> 00:02:23.827
Oh my gawd, thank you so much.

00:02:23.827 --> 00:02:26.700
- Absolutely. Thank you
for being so innovative.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:27.570
It's so cool.

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:28.590
Thank you for joining us

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.600
and also thank you to
all our guests this hour.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.250
Seth Rogan, Jessica Williams,

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.140
Meena Harris, and Lawrence Zarian

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.893
Y'all have a great day, and if
it's not, try and change it.

